IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nba-types`

-- Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK) — GOAL 1: REFUGEE STATUS UNDER
-- ARTICLE 1(A)(2) (ss 30-35). Each finding of fact is an input; the encoding
-- applies the structure the Act requires.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2022-36.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — refugee status`

DECLARE `Refugee determination` IS ONE OF
    `ss 30-35 do not apply: claim made before s 30 came into force`
    `not a refugee: no Convention reason`
    `not a refugee: stage one not met`
    `not a refugee: no reasonable likelihood of persecution`
    `not a refugee: protection is available`
    `not a refugee: internal relocation`
    `a refugee`

-- s 33(2) "A group forms a particular social group ... only if it meets both
-- of the following conditions." (3): members share an innate characteristic,
-- an unchangeable common background, or a characteristic or belief so
-- fundamental they should not be forced to renounce it; (4): a distinct
-- identity, perceived as different by the surrounding society.
@ref s 33(1)-(4)
GIVEN a IS AN `Asylum facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a Convention reason in` a IF
    CONSIDER a's `reason`
    WHEN `no Convention reason` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `membership of a particular social group` THEN
            a's `members share an innate, unchangeable or fundamental characteristic`
        AND a's `the group is perceived as different by the surrounding society`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 31(1) "persecution can be committed by ... (a) the State, (b) any party
-- or organisation controlling the State or a substantial part of the
-- territory ..., or (c) any non-State actor, if it can be demonstrated that
-- the actors mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) ... are unable or unwilling
-- to provide reasonable protection". (2): sufficiently serious.
@ref s 31(1)-(2)
GIVEN a IS AN `Asylum facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the feared harm is persecution under s 31 in` a IF
        a's `sufficiently serious to be persecution`
    AND actorCounts
    WHERE
        actorCounts MEANS
            CONSIDER a's `the actor`
            WHEN `a non-State actor` THEN a's `State and controlling parties unable or unwilling to protect`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 34(2) "An asylum seeker is to be taken to be able to avail themselves of
-- protection from persecution if— (a) the State, party or organisation ...
-- takes reasonable steps to prevent the persecution by operating an
-- effective legal system ..., and (b) the asylum seeker is able to access the
-- protection."
@ref s 34(2)
GIVEN a IS AN `Asylum facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `protection from persecution is available in` a IF
        a's `a protector operates an effective legal system against it`
    AND a's `the asylum seeker can access that protection`

-- s 30(5): ss 31-35 apply only to claims made on or after s 30 came into
-- force. s 32(2): stage one, on the balance of probabilities — the
-- characteristic and the fear. (3)-(5): stage two, a reasonable likelihood
-- of persecution and no protection (s 34), considering internal relocation
-- (s 35: not a refugee if there is no well-founded fear in another part
-- they can reasonably be expected to travel to and remain in).
@ref ss 30-35
@export Whether an asylum seeker is a refugee under Article 1(A)(2) of the Refugee Convention, decided as ss 30-35 of the Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK) require: a Convention reason (s 33, with the two-condition test for a particular social group); stage one on the balance of probabilities (the characteristic and the fear, s 32(2)); stage two on a reasonable likelihood (persecution by an actor of persecution, s 31, without available protection, s 34); and no internal relocation alternative (s 35). Each finding is an input; the result says which test failed. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN a IS AN `Asylum facts`  @desc The claim date and in-force date, and the decision-maker's findings at each stage
GIVETH A `Refugee determination`
`the refugee determination for` a MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a's `claim made on` LESS THAN a's `section 30 in force from` THEN `ss 30-35 do not apply: claim made before s 30 came into force`
        IF NOT (`there is a Convention reason in` a) THEN `not a refugee: no Convention reason`
        IF NOT (a's `has (or is attributed) the characteristic` AND a's `in fact fears persecution because of it`) THEN `not a refugee: stage one not met`
        IF NOT (a's `reasonable likelihood of persecution on return` AND `the feared harm is persecution under s 31 in` a) THEN `not a refugee: no reasonable likelihood of persecution`
        IF `protection from persecution is available in` a THEN `not a refugee: protection is available`
        IF a's `no well-founded fear in another part of the country` AND a's `can reasonably be expected to relocate there` THEN `not a refugee: internal relocation`
        OTHERWISE `a refugee`
